                <pb facs="0146" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.00/590: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De Lambert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-14T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1925—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>19. Your 28, July 10, 4 p.m. Pending crystalization of present political
                    situation you are instructed carefully to avoid any action <pb facs="0147"
                        n="65" xml:id="pg65"/> which might be construed as recognition of the regime
                    actually functioning in Ecuador. Communication with the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >de facto</hi> authorities should be friendly but personal and strictly
                    informal omitting use of titles such as Minister for Foreign Affairs, etc.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
